{{also|Liner|LINER}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlaɪnɚ/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-liner.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪnə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{af|en|line<pos:verb>|-er|id2=agent noun}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# Someone who fits a [[lining]] to something.
#: {{ux|en|a '''liner''' of shoes}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1973|author=Kyril Bonfiglioli|title=Don't Point That Thing at Me|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2001|page=41
|passage=A good '''liner''' has a pretty shrewd idea of the value of the painting he is treating and usually charges accordingly.}}
# A removable [[cover]] or [[lining]].
#: {{ux|en|I threw out the trash can '''liner'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1955|year_published=1991|author=w:J. D. Salinger|chapter=Franny|title=w:Franny and Zooey|location=Boston, Mass.|publisher=w:Little, Brown and Company|isbn=0316769495|page=3|passage=Lane Coutell, in a Burberry raincoat that apparently had a wool '''liner''' buttoned into it, was one of the six or seven boys out on the open platform.}}
# The [[pamphlet]] which is contained inside an album of music or movie.
#: {{coi|en|[[liner notes|'''liner''' notes]]}}
# A [[lining]] within the [[cylinder]] of a [[steam engine]], in which the [[piston]] works and between which and the outer shell of the cylinder a space is left to form a steam jacket.
# A similar lining for cylinders of [[internal-combustion engine]]s {{q|see "Further reading"}}.
# A [[slab]] on which small pieces of [[marble]], [[tile]], etc., are fastened for [[grind]]ing.
# A formal [[no show sock]].
# A [[pantyliner]].

